  {
   "uuid": "b9de4641-c9f1-40c0-9442-a8696e7d6c4b",
   "text": "",
   "content": [
    {
     "start_timestamp": "2026-03-16T00:33:24.757000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2026-03-16T00:33:36.713000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Then they cancel out: no education credit (nothing paid out of pocket), and no excess scholarship income. The 1098-T effectively has no effect on your return, but entering it is still the cleaner choice in case the IRS cross-checks it.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
   "sender": "assistant",
